cli-help-tune-1 = sim-cli tune MACHINE [OPTIONS]
cli-help-tune-2 = --phase-margin DEG  Least phase margin over the cycle's poses, 35 by default.
cli-help-tune-3 = --gain-margin DB  Least gain margin over the cycle's poses, 6 by default.
cli-help-tune-4 = --no-notch  Leaves the velocity loop's notch alone (otherwise tried where a resonance limits the gain).
cli-help-tune-5 = One row per key: before, after and the least margins over the poses, each with its pose. Writes no file: the --set words that make the tuned config are on the error stream. Exit code 1 where the targets are not met. tuning measures a step response and changes nothing; tune searches the gain with margins (up to 15 measurements per motor).
tune-lowered = { $arg }: the gain was lowered once more, as the other motors' tuned gains acted on it.
tune-notch = Notch kept for { $arg } (motor: centre, width, gain with it over without it).
tune-not-met = The targets are not met at every pose: the gains are the best found.
