cli-help-paths-1 = A path file has one piece per line, from where the machine stands:
cli-help-paths-2 = line,a,b  straight to the point a,b
cli-help-paths-3 = arc,a,b,ca,cb,cw|ccw  on a circle around the centre ca,cb to the point a,b
cli-help-paths-4 = spline,a,b  on a smooth curve through the point; spline lines in a row make one curve
cli-help-paths-5 = On three axes: line,x,y,z   spline,x,y,z   arc,x,y,z,cx,cy,cz,cw|ccw (in the plane of start, end, centre).
cli-help-paths-6 = Its timing is planned within the axis limits; with --time-optimal as fast as the motors allow.
cli-help-paths-7 = A file ending in .nc, .ngc, .gcode, .g, .cnc or .tap is read as G-code (G0, G1, G2, G3, F, G17/G18/G19,
cli-help-paths-8 = G20/G21, G90/G91), .src as KUKA KRL (PTP, LIN, CIRC), .mod or .prg as ABB RAPID (MoveL, MoveJ, MoveC),
cli-help-paths-9 = and lines MoveL,MoveJ,MoveC as robot moves (see docs/user-guide.md).

cli-help-units-1 = Columns and keys named in kg, N, N m, rad or rad/s hold the axis' own unit: on a linear motor N, m/s
cli-help-units-2 = and m, and the fit report's moved_mass_kg, viscous_friction_n_s_m, coulomb_friction_n and
cli-help-units-3 = constant_force_n hold kg m2, N m s/rad, N m and N m on a rotary axis.
cli-help-units-4 = Trailing columns name the units: torque_unit,speed_unit in analyze, speed_unit,torque_unit in --points,
cli-help-units-5 = torque_unit in --breakdown, search and transmission, units in fit (empty where a row has none).
cli-help-units-6 = margins leaves crossover_hz and phase_margin_deg empty where the loop has no gain crossover in the band
cli-help-units-7 = (not measurable; the result is then the gain margin's alone). modes adds mode<i>_small_hz where the
cli-help-units-8 = machine's small-amplitude modes differ (a gearbox's hysteresis). sensitivity leaves out a value of 0
